# VIVA ENGINE CONTEXT RULES
# Always run these instructions before executing anything else.

# 1. READ CONTEXT FIRST
# Never start coding or analyzing without first performing:
# - cat @current_state.md
# - cat @architecture.md
# - cat @out_of_scope.md
# - cat @decisions.md

# 2. FILE MODIFICATIONS
# - Always check @structure.txt to know where files belong.
# - Update @changelog.md with a 1-sentence summary of your action after completing a task.
# - If you finish a phase/task, update @current_state.md immediately.
# - If you make a significant architecture choice (e.g. adding a new library), update @decisions.md.

# 3. STRICT BOUNDARIES
# - DO NOT touch Lovable-generated base styling unless explicitly ordered.
# - DO NOT write custom implementations for things identified as open-source in @decisions.md (e.g., spaced repetition, audio transcription).
# - NEVER commit backend/.env.

# 4. GIT WORKFLOW
# - Never work directly on `main`.
# - Use `git checkout -b phase-<N>/<feature-name>`
# - Run Python backend: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`
# - Run Frontend: `npm run dev`
